      "writtenOn": "2022-02-03T00:14:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks. For now I think #2 is the best option. Longer term, #4 is much better. The ConnectivityManager API takes an int firewall chain, then it converts that into a string, then it passes it to trafficcontroller via the IPC, then the string is converted back into an int.\n\nWe should definitely simplify that, though not sure how much we can simplify it given that we also have to support S. I suppose we can at least change all the code to pass around integers and only hide the complexity in BpfNetMaps.\n\nCould you also upload a CL to deprecate the constants and methods in INetd.aidl that the code has now moved away from?",
